# Ansible Task Key Order

In every Ansible task (including `include_role` / `import_role` tasks),
place `when` directly after `name`, before the module/action keyword and
its `vars`/args.

```yaml
# ✅ GOOD
- name: Install kafka
  when: "'kafka' in install_apps"
  ansible.builtin.include_role:
    name: cloud.apps.kafka
  vars:
    kafka_mode: "{{ _kafka_mode | default('zookeeper') }}"
```

```yaml
# ❌ BAD — when trails after the module/vars
- name: Install kafka
  ansible.builtin.include_role:
    name: cloud.apps.kafka
  vars:
    kafka_mode: "{{ _kafka_mode | default('zookeeper') }}"
  when: "'kafka' in install_apps"
```

This is a project style preference, not an ansible-lint requirement —
both orderings pass `ansible-lint --profile production`. Apply this
ordering to new/edited tasks; don't mass-reorder unrelated existing tasks
in the same change.
